<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Bid lifts lid on Leutennegger shares.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Bid lifts lid on Leutennegger shares.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in hatmaker Leutennegger Ltd jumped nearly 60 percent to 30 cents on Wednesday following Hancock &amp; Gore Ltd's scrip bid.</p>
<p>Hancock &amp; Gore said on Tuesday it would offer one of its shares for every four Leutennegger shares, valuing the company at about A$5.6 million or 32.5 cents per share.</p>
<p>The stock ended at 19 cents prior to the bid.</p>
<p>The bid caps a turbulent time for the Brisbane-based milliner since listing in November 1993 at A$1.04. Its shares sank to a low of 15 cents in May 1996 amid boardroom turmoil and resignations. -- Walter Watson 61-2 9373 1810</p>
</text>
